<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Graphics on Gabriel H. Brown</title><link>https://ghbrown.net/tags/graphics/</link><description>Recent content in Graphics on Gabriel H. Brown</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><copyright>Copyright [Gabriel H. Brown](/).</copyright><lastBuildDate>Sat, 21 Nov 2026 02:19:38 -0600</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://ghbrown.net/tags/graphics/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Computing the eigenfunctions of my fat head</title><link>https://ghbrown.net/posts/head_eigenfunctions/</link><pubDate>Sat, 21 Nov 2026 02:19:38 -0600</pubDate><guid>https://ghbrown.net/posts/head_eigenfunctions/</guid><description>&lt;h1 id="computing-the-eigenfunctions-of-my-fat-head"&gt;Computing the eigenfunctions of my fat head&lt;/h1&gt;&#10;&lt;hr&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;This is the basic workflow of how I generated the animation below (also on the homepage of this website) using only open source software.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10; &#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;video id="bust"&#10; style="width:100%;aspect-ratio:1;"&#10; title=""&#10; alt="rotating mesh of my shoulders and head" autoplay loop muted playsinline&#10;&gt;&lt;/video&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;video id="canary"&#10; muted playsinline&#10; preload="auto"&#10; aria-hidden="true"&#10; style="position:fixed;left:0;top:0;width:32px;height:32px;opacity:0;pointer-events:none"&gt;&#10;&lt;/video&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;canvas id="probe" width="32" height="32" hidden&gt;&lt;/canvas&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;script&gt;&#10; const vid = document.getElementById("bust");&#10; const canary = document.getElementById("canary");&#10; const canvas = document.getElementById("probe");&#10; const ctx = canvas.getContext("2d", { willReadFrequently: true });&#10;&#10; let usingMp4 = false;&#10;&#10; function useMp4() {&#10; if (usingMp4) return;&#10; usingMp4 = true;&#10; vid.src = "\/assets\/bust.mp4";&#10; vid.load();&#10; vid.play().catch(() =&gt; {});&#10; }&#10;&#10; function useWebm() {&#10; vid.src = "\/assets\/bust.webm";&#10; vid.load();&#10; vid.play().catch(() =&gt; {});&#10; }&#10;&#10;&#10; function testCanary() {&#10; ctx.drawImage(canary, 0, 0, 32, 32);&#10; const leftAlpha = ctx.getImageData(8, 16, 1, 1).data[3];&#10; const rightAlpha = ctx.getImageData(24, 16, 1, 1).data[3];&#10; canary.pause();&#10;&#10; if (leftAlpha &gt; 240 &amp;&amp; rightAlpha &lt; 16) {&#10; &#10; useWebm();&#10; } else {&#10; &#10; useMp4();&#10; }&#10; }&#10;&#10; let checked = false;&#10; function checkCanaryOnce() {&#10; if (checked) return; &#10; checked = true;&#10; testCanary();&#10; }&#10;&#10; &#10; vid.addEventListener("error", useMp4);&#10; canary.addEventListener("error", useMp4, { once: true });&#10;&#10; &#10; if ("requestVideoFrameCallback" in canary) {&#10; &#10; canary.requestVideoFrameCallback(checkCanaryOnce);&#10; } else {&#10; canary.addEventListener("loadeddata", () =&gt; {&#10; requestAnimationFrame(checkCanaryOnce);&#10; }, { once: true });&#10; }&#10;&#10; &#10; canary.src = "/assets/alpha-test.webm";&#10; canary.load();&#10; canary.play().catch(useMp4);&#10;&lt;/script&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;In one sentence:&#10;I used &#10;&lt;a href="https://colmap.github.io/" target="_blank"&gt;COLMAP&lt;/a&gt; and &#10;&lt;a href="https://github.com/openMVG/openMVG" target="_blank"&gt;OpenMVG&lt;/a&gt; to generate a textured mesh of myself from pictures;&#10;then I used &#10;&lt;a href="https://libigl.github.io/" target="_blank"&gt;libigl&lt;/a&gt;, &#10;&lt;a href="https://scipy.org/" target="_blank"&gt;scipy&lt;/a&gt;, and &#10;&lt;a href="https://trimesh.org/" target="_blank"&gt;trimesh&lt;/a&gt; to compute an eigenfunction and generate a corresponding texture;&#10;then I used &#10;&lt;a href="https://www.blender.org/" target="_blank"&gt;Blender&lt;/a&gt; to overlay the textures and make the final render.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Transparent videos from Blender to the web</title><link>https://ghbrown.net/posts/alpha_video/</link><pubDate>Sat, 13 Jul 2024 12:37:01 -0500</pubDate><guid>https://ghbrown.net/posts/alpha_video/</guid><description>&lt;h1 id="get-transparent-videos-out-of-blender-and-onto-the-web"&gt;Get transparent videos out of Blender and onto the web&lt;/h1&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;A quick guide to get your cool render out of Blender and onto the web, with transparency/alpha!&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;hr&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="out-of-blender"&gt;Out of &#10;&lt;a href="https://www.blender.org/" target="_blank"&gt;Blender&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;For renders to intermediate frame images you can use the following Blender settings in the Properties Editor:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;pre tabindex="0"&gt;&lt;code&gt;Render &amp;gt; Film &amp;gt; Transparent (check it)&#10;Output &amp;gt; Output &amp;gt; File Format &amp;gt; PNG&#10;Output &amp;gt; Output &amp;gt; Color &amp;gt; RGBA&#10;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;p&gt;For a small renders directly to video files (bad practice) I used the following settings:&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>